---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import "@/styles/content.css";

const title = "Terms of use — School Skills";
const description =
  "Plain-language terms for using School Skills. Free to use, provided as-is, and your progress is yours.";
const updated = "12 August 2026";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="page">
    <p class="page__eyebrow">Terms of use</p>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="page__lead">
      Short, because there isn't much to agree to — there's no account, no
      payment and nothing of yours held anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Using the site</h2>
    <p>
      School Skills is free for personal, family, classroom and school use. Play
      it, share it, put it on the board — no permission needed and no
      attribution required.
    </p>

    <h2>Your progress is yours</h2>
    <p>
      Everything the app saves lives in your browser on your device. We never
      receive it, so we can't view it, sell it, lose it, or give it back if it's
      gone. Use the <strong>Back up progress</strong> button if it matters to you.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided as-is. It's a learning game built with care, not a
      certified assessment tool — don't rely on it as a measure of a child's
      attainment, and don't rely on the browser to keep saved progress forever.
      Browsers clear storage: in private windows always, and on iOS after a
      period of not visiting the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      There is no guarantee the site stays online or unchanged. Games may be
      added, altered or removed.
    </p>

    <h2>Content</h2>
    <p>
      The games, text and design are ours. The mathematics is not — nobody owns
      the seven times table.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:hello@schoolskills.app">hello@schoolskills.app</a></p>

    <footer class="page__foot">
      <a href="/">School Skills</a>
      <a href="/flash-cards">Flash cards</a>
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
